       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **Ordered:** 1600 mg four times daily, which is 6,400 mg/day.\n- **Maximum dose:** The maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day for prescription use, given as up to 800 mg per dose. The OTC limit is 1,200 mg/day.\n- **Risk:** This order is twice the daily maximum, and each dose is twice the single-dose maximum. That raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the usual maximum for inflammatory conditions.\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours**, or **800 mg PO three times daily**, for typical analgesic or anti-inflammatory use.\n- **1600 mg/day total**, for example 400 mg four times daily, if the figure was meant as a daily total.\n\nIf you really do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first. Once you confirm the dose, I'll enter the order."
      }
